<title>LATVIA: RIETUMU BACKED BY COURT IN ST PETERSBURG TAX ROW.</title>
<headline>RIETUMU BACKED BY COURT IN ST PETERSBURG TAX ROW.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rietumu Bank said on Friday that a St Petersburg court has ordered the city's tax police not to intefere with its correspondent accounts in the city and that it expected to resume normal work in Russia.</p>
<p>&quot;We are certain that after this decision...will come other, similar decisions and that the artificially created obstacles to the normal work of Baltic banks in Russia will be ended,&quot; the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>Rietumu was one of the several Latvian, Lithuanian and Estonian banks which had their correspondent accounts frozen in St Petersburg by the tax police for non-payment of VAT.</p>
<p>Estonia's Forekspank and Tallinna Pank said earlier that they have also had decisions in their favour by the St Petersburg arbitration court.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
